keywords:
  - forest fire early warning
  - probability calibration
  - spatial cross-validation
  - cost-loss analysis
  - risk ranking
  - Yunnan
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a calibrated machine-learning framework that ranks
  satellite-detectable forest fire hotspots on 0.1 degree forest grids in Yunnan,
  China. The framework links temporal extrapolation, isotonic calibration, simple
  baselines, five-fold spatial holdout, and cost-loss decision analysis. It supports
  retrospective risk ranking, not real-time forecasting or resource dispatch.
